# A3 step 3 planner S5 F1 giver prefilter (twow-repo#726; F1-ENTWURF-v0.2, OB-60 pre-review, OB-10 OK 0c2f2727;
# AiPlayerbot.Planner.GiverPrefilter / GiverPrefilterVerify, default 0). Pinned here:
#   (a) GiverPrefilterPolicy.h is pure and has no distance formula of its own (only min, add, compare: no coordinate, no
#       sqDistance, no pow / fma), so the bound can not drift from the original by an ulp;
#   (b) WorldWpSquare::SqDistanceLowerBound takes every term from the original functions (IsIn / sqOutDistance of the map square,
#       the portal list of the fetch) and the original distance functions are unchanged (byte pins);
#   (c) TravelMgr: the switch is a thread-local pointer, null by default; the condition (switch, !onlyPossible, a radius); the
#       check in both walk paths right after the start-zone check and before the traced range / IsPossible; the portal cache is
#       call-local; no other source file names the switch;
#   (d) PlannerShadow: the switch only around the giver fetch, by a scope that always clears it; the cohort rule; the verify
#       runs the original list with both thread pointers null;
#   (e) the keys: read, GiverPrefilter above 3 is 0 with one error line, both echoed (sorted), documented = 0, in the planner key
#       list; the [PlanTime] suffix only with the prefilter;
#   (f) the unit suite giver_prefilter_policy is registered and runs every test.
# Every check_* returns "" when it holds, else the reason; the negative probes at the end reuse them on mutated text.
